  "43": {"title":"The Jones Act of 1920","year":"2024","details":"Viejo San Juan, PR · 35mm","description":"The Jones Act, Section 27 of the Merchant Marine Act (46 U.S.C. § 55102), prohibits the transport of merchandise by water between points in the United States in any vessel that is not U.S.-built, U.S.-owned, and U.S.-documented. In Puerto Rico's case, this drives up the price of nearly everything sold here, slowly strangling an island that once sustained itself.","tags":["Film Photography","35mm Film","Color Photography","Harbor","Ocean","Social Commentary","History","Jones Act","Shipping","Economy"]},
