  "80": {"title":"Money","year":"2025","details":"New York City, NY · 35mm","description":"A widely accepted medium of exchange, unit of account, and store of value. In the United States, the Federal Reserve issues the dollar and the Treasury prints and mints it. The dollar is backed by the full faith and credit of the U.S. government, the same government that passed $40 trillion in debt in August 2026 and now borrows to pay the interest on what it already owes.","tags":["Film Photography","35mm Film","Color Photography","Street Photography","Social Commentary","Money","Economy","Debt","Lucas","Suau"]},
