  "83": {"title":"Upkeep","year":"2025","details":"New York City, NY · 35mm","description":"A city is a cathedral of industry that never sleeps, and it does not mend itself. Beneath its spires and along its arteries, unseen laborers perform the endless rites of upkeep, patching iron veins, soothing tired machines, and holding back the slow tide of rust and ruin. Their work is never finished and rarely seen, yet without it, the great engine of the city would falter and fall silent.","tags":["Film Photography","35mm Film","B&W Photography","Street Photography","Workers","Social Commentary","Infrastructure","Maintenance"]},
